Credits
=======

QStep glues together the work of many others: LinuxCNC; Arduino (UNO Q
hardware, Debian image, linux-qcom kernel, Zephyr fork, ArduinoCore-zephyr,
OpenOCD setup, Flasher CLI); the Linux kernel, PREEMPT_RT and Qualcomm/Linaro
mainline developers; Zephyr, STMicroelectronics and Arm CMSIS; Remora (Scott
Alford) and the Mesa/LinuxCNC stepgen design, whose ideas are reused but not
their code; Debian, OpenOCD and Lima. Much of QStep was developed with
Claude (Anthropic) as an AI coding assistant. See "Standing on the shoulders
of giants" in README.md.

