Prebuilt files in dist/
=======================

dist/kernel/linux-image-6.16.0-rt-qstep1_1_arm64.deb
dist/kernel/linux-headers-6.16.0-rt-qstep1_1_arm64.deb
    Linux kernel, GPL-2.0-only. Corresponding source:
    https://github.com/arduino/linux-qcom at commit
    effa8626771ad31536aafd3a5aa94cad7e528e23, plus kernel/rt.config and
    kernel/patches/ from this repository. Built with kernel/build-rt-kernel.sh
    from the base configuration in kernel/config-6.16.0-geffa8626771a.stock.

dist/hal/unoq_spi.so
    QStep HAL driver for LinuxCNC (GPL-2.0-or-later), built from hal/unoq_spi.c
    against the LinuxCNC 2.9.4 headers (linuxcnc-uspace-dev, Debian 13).
    LinuxCNC is free software under the GPL; see https://linuxcnc.org.

dist/firmware/qstep-fw.elf, dist/firmware/qstep-fw.bin
    STM32U585 firmware built from firmware/qstep-fw and firmware/common (this
    repository) and linked with:
      - the Zephyr RTOS, Arduino fork https://github.com/arduino/zephyr, tag
        zephyr-arduino-v4.4.1+ (Apache-2.0)
      - CMSIS (Apache-2.0)
      - the STM32Cube HAL/LL drivers from zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32
        (BSD-3-Clause, LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt)
    Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPL version 3 but not with version 2.
    QStep's firmware sources are GPL-2.0-or-later, so the combined firmware
    image is distributed under the GNU GPL version 3 or later
    (LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt). The Apache-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause
    notices above apply to the corresponding parts.

Not included
============

QStep doesn't redistribute Arduino's UNO Q system image, its Qualcomm boot
firmware, or Arduino's STM32 firmware. Users flash Arduino's official image
with Arduino's own tools (see dist/README.md).

